{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **November 6, 2026**:\n\n- **Start with the issuer’s official ETF website**, usually “Holdings” or “Download holdings.” [Rule 6c-11](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11) requires public daily disclosure, before trading opens, of portfolio holdings underlying the next NAV calculation, including identifiers, quantities and portfolio weights. Check the file’s as-of date.\n- **For the actual portfolio composition file (PCF)**, contact the sponsor’s ETF capital-markets or creation/redemption desk. Specify the date, creation versus redemption, and standard versus custom basket. Ask whether they can supply it directly or through a broker, authorized participant, or licensed data vendor. Access may require permission or fees; retail access is not guaranteed.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Holdings describe the investment portfolio; transaction baskets describe securities and cash exchanged for ETF shares. They can differ materially. Rule 6c-11’s holdings disclosure requirement does **not** guarantee a free public PCF."}}
